  <div class="row-body">
    <div class="row-ruler" id="rowRuler" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="content-col">

      <header class="hero" id="profile">
        <h1>Emmanuel Abolade</h1>
        <p class="role">Data Analyst / Business Intelligence &amp; Full-Stack Developer</p>
        <p class="lede">I take operational and performance data from raw tables to a decision: clean it, define the KPI from the source field, check the grain before joining, and recommend only what the evidence supports. Based in Hull, UK.</p>
        <p class="lede">The same discipline shows up when I build software. Booking flows, admin approval, and executive BI screens are treated like analytical products: clear entities, honest constraints, and interfaces that surface exceptions instead of hiding them.</p>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="mailto:aboladeanuoluwapo@gmail.com">Email Emmanuel Abolade</a>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/emmanuel-aboladesek" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn profile</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/aboladvisuals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub profile</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <main>
      <section id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
        <p class="section-label">B2</p>
        <h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>

        <article class="job">
          <div class="job-top">
            <span class="job-title">Data Analyst — Amdari</span>
            <span class="job-date">United Kingdom · 2025–Present</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Analyse business datasets to identify trends, patterns and performance gaps using Excel, Power Query, SQL, Python and R.</li>
            <li>Develop analytical reports and dashboards in Power BI and Excel; build KPIs and performance metrics.</li>
            <li>Query structured and relational datasets using SQL, including a three-table NHS A&amp;E analysis.</li>
            <li>Present findings to stakeholders via dashboards, reports and stakeholder meetings.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="job">
          <div class="job-top">
            <span class="job-title">Data Analyst — Pinntech Ltd</span>
            <span class="job-date">United Kingdom · 2024–2025</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Cleaned and transformed data using Excel, Power Query and SQL; performed validation and quality checks.</li>
            <li>Queried and aggregated relational data, including a 191-row NHS A&amp;E activity dataset.</li>
            <li>Built PowerPoint presentations and presented directly in stakeholder meetings.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="job">
          <div class="job-top">
            <span class="job-title">Freelance — Data Annotation, Outlier AI, Handshake</span>
            <span class="job-date">Remote · Current</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Light, ongoing freelance work in data annotation / AI evaluation and full stack development tasks.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="how-i-work" aria-labelledby="how-i-work-heading">
        <p class="section-label">C3</p>
        <h2 id="how-i-work-heading">How I Work</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Analysis and software share one standard: define the question, respect the grain, enforce constraints, and only ship claims the evidence supports.</p>

        <h3>Analytical practice</h3>
        <ol class="workflow">
          <li>Start from the business decision, not the chart.</li>
          <li>Profile source tables and document grain before joins.</li>
          <li>Clean and validate with explicit rules; keep exclusions auditable.</li>
          <li>Define KPIs from source fields, not preferred narratives.</li>
          <li>Cross-check findings in more than one tool when the stake is high.</li>
          <li>Recommend actions only where the evidence is strong enough to act.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Data → software</h3>
        <p class="section-intro" style="margin-top:0;">Restaurant financial analysis became ControlDeck NG — a productised UI over the same control gaps. Booking demand became Bibiunique — availability API, unique slot constraint, and admin approval instead of inbox chaos. Analysis that stops at a slide deck leaves the operational problem unsolved; software that ignores grain and validation invents confidence.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="data-bi" aria-labelledby="data-bi-heading">
        <p class="section-label">D4</p>
        <h2 id="data-bi-heading">Data &amp; BI</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Selected analytics and business-intelligence case studies. Metrics below are from the project repositories and published write-ups.</p>

